# miaw-core / miaw-cli runtime configuration
#
# Copy to .env and edit. Every value here is optional — each has a default and
# each can also be supplied as a CLI flag. Flags win over environment variables.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Prefer this file over CLI flags for anything containing a
# password: flags land in your shell history and in the process list, where any
# other user on the machine can read them.

# ─── Instance ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Instance ID. Sessions are isolated per instance. (flag: --instance-id)
MIAW_INSTANCE_ID=default

# Where session credentials are stored, as {MIAW_SESSION_PATH}/{MIAW_INSTANCE_ID}/
# (flag: --session-path)
MIAW_SESSION_PATH=./sessions-cli

# ─── Proxy (all optional; added in v1.10.0) ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Precedence, highest first (v1.11.0):
#   1. MIAW_PROXY / --proxy        always wins; warns when it shadows a pin
#   2. a pin in <MIAW_SESSION_PATH>/instances.json, per instance
#   3. MIAW_PROXY_FILE + strategy  hashed on the TARGET instanceId
#   4. direct
#
# The pin store is written by `miaw-cli instance set-proxy <id> ...`, not by
# env vars - it is per-instance state, so it belongs with the sessions rather
# than with process config. It holds credentials when a URL is pinned, so it is
# written 0600 and must live on the same persistent, secret-grade volume as the
# session directories. See docs/DEPLOYMENT_INSTANCE_PROXY.md.

# A single proxy for this instance. (flag: --proxy)
# Schemes: http, https, socks4, socks4a, socks5, socks5h
#
# Prefer the h/a variants (socks5h, socks4a): plain socks5/socks4 resolve DNS
# locally, so the destination hostname leaks to your resolver even though the
# connection itself is tunnelled.
#
# Passwords containing @ : / ? # or % must be percent-encoded here
# ("p@ss#1" becomes "p%40ss%231"), or use the ProxyConfig object form in code.
#
# MIAW_PROXY=socks5h://user:password@proxy.example.com:1080

# A proxy list file instead of a single proxy — TXT (one per line) or JSON
# array. A proxy is selected per instance using MIAW_PROXY_STRATEGY, keyed on
# the instance the command targets (v1.11.0; before that, once per process
# against the startup instance).
# Ignored when MIAW_PROXY is also set, and outranked by a per-instance pin.
# (flag: --proxy-file)
#
# Also required when an instance is pinned by label (`instance set-proxy <id>
# --label eu`): the label names an entry in THIS file. A label pin that cannot
# be resolved refuses to connect rather than silently going direct.
#
# See examples/proxies.example.txt for the format.
#
# MIAW_PROXY_FILE=./proxies.txt

# How a proxy is picked from MIAW_PROXY_FILE. (flag: --proxy-strategy)
#   deterministic  same instanceId always maps to the same proxy   [default]
#   round-robin    next in the list, wrapping
#   random         uniform random
#   weighted       random, biased by each entry's weight=
#
# Leave this as deterministic for anything with a persisted WhatsApp session.
# WhatsApp treats a session's source IP as a trust signal, so a session whose
# egress IP jumps between runs looks like an account takeover. Rotation is for
# spreading instances across proxies, never for rotating a live session's IP.
#
# MIAW_PROXY_STRATEGY=deterministic

# ─── Logging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Verbose Baileys logging. (flag: --debug)
# DEBUG=false
